    "content": "Ayurvedic Dashavidha Pariksha Diagnostic Criteria: 1. Prakriti & Vikriti: Evaluation of baseline biological constitution (Vata, Pitta, Kapha) versus current pathological imbalance. 2. Jwara (Febrile state) is predominantly characterized by Amadosha (endotoxin accumulation) and Mandagni (suppression of metabolic fire). 3. In Pitta-dominant Jwara with burning sensation, thirst, and sour eructations (Amlapitta correlation), Langhana (digestive rest), Shadanga Paniya, and mild cooling/digestive herbs are recommended. 4. Agni State: Mandagni dictates light easily digestible food (Manda, Peya) and avoidance of heavy dairy or greasy food until digestive fire stabilizes.",
    "entity_type": "guideline",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "CCRAS AYUSH Dashavidha Pariksha & Jwara Assessment",
      "category": "ayush_integrative",
      "source": "CCRAS Ayurvedic Clinical Protocol Handbook"
    },
    "updated_at": 1790708007.522756
  },
