    "content": "Protocol for Acid Peptic Disorders & Amlapitta: 1. Symptoms: Postprandial burning sensation in epigastrium, sour regurgitation, retrosternal heartburn, and nausea. 2. First-line therapy: Proton Pump Inhibitors (Pantoprazole 40mg or Omeprazole 20mg once daily taken 30 minutes before breakfast) for 2 to 4 weeks. 3. AYUSH correlation: Pitta-Vata aggravation. Dietary rules: avoid pungent (Katu), sour (Amla), fermented foods and late-night meals. Cooling herbs like Yashtimadhu, Shatavari, and Amalaki support mucosal healing.",
    "entity_type": "guideline",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "Clinical Management of Dyspepsia, GERD & Amlapitta",
      "category": "gastroenterology",
      "source": "Indian Society of Gastroenterology Clinical Consensus"
    },
    "updated_at": 1790708007.524322
  },
